{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"nubuck-wailsome-bronco","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nWhen no OS sandbox mechanism is available, `mutation_sandbox.wrap()` proceeds\nUNSANDBOXED with a warning if the ambient `CI` environment variable is truthy, and\naborts otherwise. `CI` is inheritable and trivially set, so a workstation with `CI=1`\nexported — say, while debugging a CI script — silently runs mutation tests with no\nsandbox. That is the configuration the 2026-08-26 incident happened in.\n\nAmbient `CI` is currently the SOLE condition on that fail-open.\n\n## Why it was left this way\n\nThe `CI` convention is deliberate and correct for portability: it names no provider, so\nthe fallback works on any CI system (`project.portability`). The problem is not that\n`CI` is consulted; it is that nothing else is. `baf9-eea0` improved the WARNING so a run\nthat takes this path is unmistakable in its log, but explicitly did not change the gate.\n\nSince `0d22-f664` the Linux lane has a working `bwrap` and macOS has `sandbox-exec`, so\nthe fallback should now be rare — which makes tightening it cheap to try and easy to\nobserve.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The unsandboxed fail-open requires an EXPLICIT project opt-in in addition to\n      ambient `CI` — e.g. a config key defaulting to off — so exporting `CI=1` on a\n      workstation is not sufficient to disable the sandbox. Verified by a test asserting\n      that with `CI` truthy, no mechanism, and the opt-in absent, the run ABORTS.\n- [ ] With the opt-in present and `CI` truthy, the run proceeds unsandboxed with the\n      existing warning. Verified by a test.\n- [ ] The opt-in names no CI provider (`project.portability`).\n- [ ] Every lane that currently relies on the fallback is identified before the default\n      flips, and the change is shown not to break them — a lane that silently starts\n      aborting is a worse outcome than the gap being closed.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- Ambient `CI` alone can no longer disable the sandbox.\n- The blast radius on existing lanes is enumerated, not assumed.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`.\n\n## Notes\n\nSplit from `baf9-eea0` during its plan review, which correctly refused a criterion that\nclaimed to require \"more than ambient CI alone\" while verifying only warning text.\nSeparated because changing this gate is a behaviour change affecting every lane that\nrelies on the fallback, and deserves its own review rather than riding along in a\ndocs-and-messages cleanup. Discovered from `e668-b496`.","id":"f11d-f8fd-5860-448d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Ambient CI alone can disable the mutation sandbox"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787892957220560001,"uuid":"25b974c8-c9db-4cf1-b0c2-ee8cc2231eec"}